Patch 2009: a display-sized texture that is an offscreen render target is no longer sampled from the screen copy.

The pre-pass bound the previous frame copy to every sampler whose texture is as large as the display, before it looked for an
offscreen render target with that offset. The 3D title scene is drawn into a 1280x720 target that the post chain samples, so the
post chain read the wrong image. The offscreen target now wins.

--- a/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_d3d12_backend.c
@@ -4963,7 +4963,8 @@
             }
             /* Display-sized sampler source -> the rendered frame. */
             if (dr->tex[_u].set && s_screen_copy &&
-                dr->tex[_u].w == s_d3d.width && dr->tex[_u].h == s_d3d.height) {
+                dr->tex[_u].w == s_d3d.width && dr->tex[_u].h == s_d3d.height &&
+                off_rt_find(dr->tex[_u].raw) < 0) {   /* a display-sized offscreen RT is its own producer */
                 static int en = -1;
                 if (en < 0) { const char* e = getenv("SCREEN_AS_TEX"); en = e ? atoi(e) : 1; }
                 if (en) {
